<article class="env-lemma" id="05B2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05B2">Lemma <span data-tag="05B2">35.7.6</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $\{ f_ i : X_ i \to X\} _{i \in I}$ be an fpqc covering such that each $f_ i^*\mathcal{F}$ is a finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_{X_ i}$-module. Then $\mathcal{F}$ is a finite locally free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the fact that a quasi-coherent sheaf is finite locally free if and only if it is of finite presentation and flat, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00NX" data-tag="00NX">10.78.2</a>. Namely, if each $f_ i^*\mathcal{F}$ is flat and of finite presentation, then so is $\mathcal{F}$ by Lemmas <a href="/tag/05B1" data-tag="05B1">35.7.5</a> and <a href="/tag/05B0" data-tag="05B0">35.7.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>